cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "This software citation is prepared for v1.0.0; the release and Zenodo DOI are pending. Cite the archived version when available."
type: software
title: "sagarmatha-microbiome-analysis: analytical and reproducibility code for the Sagarmatha (Mount Everest) microbiome study"
version: 1.0.0
authors:
  - given-names: Alex
    family-names: Prima
    email: "alexprima@student.ub.ac.id"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4773-8777"
    affiliation: "Universitas Brawijaya (doctoral student); BRIN (research assistant)"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Journal-associated analytical and reproducibility software for the Sagarmatha
  (Mount Everest) longitudinal gut microbiome study. This code repository provides
  reviewed analytical workflows, configuration, environment definitions, validation
  materials and supporting technical documentation for per-MAG mixed models,
  diversity, subject-aware Random Forest validation, exploratory NetMoss and
  predicted functional potential analyses. Underlying research data, participant
  metadata, generated scientific results and private development history are not
  distributed. Scientific reproduction requires separately obtained authorized inputs.
keywords:
  - longitudinal microbiome
  - Everest
  - metagenome-assembled genomes
  - mixed models
  - reproducible research
